---
slug: sign-in/code
method: post
layout: ''
searchable: false
metadata: {
    page_name: "Sign In With Code - Submit",
}
---

{%- liquid
  if context.current_user
    redirect_to '/dashboard'
    break
  endif

  comment
    A post without a valid authenticity token is not refused: it arrives with an empty
    session. The form page sets this flag, so its absence means the token was missing or wrong.
  endcomment
  if context.session.sign_in_form != 'on'
    redirect_to '/sign-in/code?error=session'
    break
  endif

  assign email = context.params.email | default: '' | strip | downcase
  assign code = context.params.code | default: '' | append: '' | remove: ' ' | strip
  graphql remembered = 'account/create_session', name: 'sign_in_code_email', value: email

  comment
    A code is exactly 6 digits. Anything else is refused before it can use a guess.
  endcomment
  assign non_digits = code | replace_regex: '[0-9]', ''
  if email == blank or code.size != 6 or non_digits != blank
    redirect_to '/sign-in/code?error=invalid'
    break
  endif

  comment
    Across all codes for one address: 10 wrong codes, or 50 from one IP address, in an
    hour stop further checks. Only wrong codes are recorded (below). Within one code,
    the 5 try slots are the limit, and they hold even under concurrent requests.
  endcomment
  function allowed = 'account/rate_limit/allow', action: 'sign_in_code_check', key: email, max_per_key: 10, max_per_ip: 50, window: 3600, count_only: true
  unless allowed
    redirect_to '/sign-in/code?error=too_many'
    break
  endunless

  comment
    Only the newest request for the address counts. A request with no account (miss) goes
    through exactly the same steps as a real one, expiry and try slots included, and is
    refused only at the end, so the answers never tell which addresses have accounts.
  endcomment
  graphql found = 'account/sign_in/find_code_request', email: email
  assign request = found.requests.results | first
  assign now_unix = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign result = 'invalid'
  assign checked = false
  assign guess = 0

  if request.status == 'killed'
    assign result = 'too_many'
  elsif request.status == 'pending' or request.status == 'miss'
    assign expires_unix = request.expires_at | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    if expires_unix <= now_unix
      assign result = 'expired'
    else
      assign checked = true
    endif
  endif

  if checked
    comment
      Every guess first claims one of 5 try slots. A right code then claims the single use
      slot, so neither the guess limit nor "works once" can be beaten by sending many
      requests at once.
    endcomment
    function guess = 'account/sign_in/take_slot', table: 'sign_in_code', key: request.id, label: 'try', count: 5
    if guess == 0
      assign result = 'too_many'
    else
      function code_hash = 'account/sign_in/code_hash', email: email, code: code
      function account = 'account/sign_in/allowed_user', email: email
      if code_hash != blank and code_hash == request.code_hash and request.status == 'pending' and account.id != blank
        comment
          After 3 2FA lockouts in 24 hours the account needs a password reset, the same as
          for password sign-in. Check it before the code is used, so the code still works
          once the password has been reset. Only someone who has the right code gets this
          answer, so it tells nobody else anything.
        endcomment
        function reset_required = 'account/two_factor_reset_required', user_id: account.id
        if reset_required
          assign result = 'reset'
        else
          function used = 'account/sign_in/take_slot', table: 'sign_in_code', key: request.id, label: 'use', count: 1
          if used == 1
            assign result = 'ok'
          endif
        endif
      endif
      if result == 'invalid'
        function recorded = 'account/rate_limit/record', action: 'sign_in_code_check', key: email, window: 3600
      endif
    endif

    comment
      A wrong fifth guess, or no try slot left, ends the request: the right code after it
      is refused too, and the person asks for a new one.
    endcomment
    assign kill = false
    if result == 'too_many'
      assign kill = true
    elsif result == 'invalid' and guess == 5
      assign kill = true
    endif
    if kill
      graphql killed = 'account/sign_in/set_request_status', table: 'sign_in_code', id: request.id, from: request.status, to: 'killed'
      assign result = 'too_many'
    endif
  endif

  if result != 'ok'
    assign goto = '/sign-in/code?error=' | append: result
    redirect_to goto
    break
  endif

  graphql consumed = 'account/sign_in/set_request_status', table: 'sign_in_code', id: request.id, from: 'pending', to: 'consumed'
  graphql cleared_email = 'account/delete_session', name: 'sign_in_code_email'

  comment
    2FA is passed per session. Clear any earlier value before signing in, so this sign-in
    has to pass 2FA again when the account has it turned on.
  endcomment
  graphql cleared_2fa = 'account/delete_session', name: 'two_factor_user_id'
  sign_in user_id: account.id

  function goto = 'account/sign_in/destination', otp_configured: account.otp_configured, return_to: request.return_to
  redirect_to goto
-%}
